<item><title>Burundi city disrupted by blaring advertisements</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-city-disrupted-by-blaring-advertisements-ae1d77/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-city-disrupted-by-blaring-advertisements-ae1d77/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Loud, repetitive advertising panels in Gitega are causing economic losses and health concerns for residents and businesses.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:21:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi police hold 21 residents over fertiliser protest</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-police-hold-21-residents-over-fertiliser-protest-28be5c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-police-hold-21-residents-over-fertiliser-protest-28be5c/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>At least 21 people, including four women and three infants, remain in custody after a dispute over fertiliser distribution in Gitega province.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:37:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-police-hold-21-residents-over-fertiliser-protest-28be5c/share.jpg" length="38967" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-police-hold-21-residents-over-fertiliser-protest-28be5c/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi arrests prison director and two officials over businessman&apos;s privileges</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-arrests-prison-director-and-two-officials-over-00d5e7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-arrests-prison-director-and-two-officials-over-00d5e7/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>The three Mpimba prison officials are held by the National Intelligence Service (SNR), accused of granting special treatment to a businessman linked to trade in M23-controlled.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:26:11 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
